# The four surfaces mnml ships itself (src/app/integrations.zig's
# `first_party`): no manifest describes them, so nothing scans them in —
# the Installed tab lists them above whatever is installed, always, and a
# fresh data root reads `Inst (4)` instead of the `Inst (0)` the
# walkthrough found (finding 1). Each row carries its `first-party`
# badge; Claude's and Codex's second line is the usage reader's quota
# rather than a command id. The row menu reaches the surface: Enter on
# Claude Code's *Usage* opens the usage pane.
command view.activity_integrations
expect screen contains INTEGRATIONS
expect screen contains "Inst (4)"
expect screen lacks "Nothing installed yet"
# The column is 26 cells at the shipped width, so the badge clips like
# every other badge does; a drag on the divider reads the whole row.
expect screen contains "Browser"
expect screen contains "browser.open"
drag 30 5 70 5
expect screen contains "Browser  first-party"
expect screen contains "Claude Code (hidden)  first-party"
expect screen contains "Codex (hidden)  first-party"
expect screen contains "HTTP (hidden)  first-party"
expect screen contains "view.activity_http"
# No account on file: the AI rows say why there is no number.
expect screen contains "not logged in"
# Browser's menu: its own action, then the two preferences.
rightclick 4 5
expect screen contains "Open"
expect screen contains "Disable"
# Browser is the one chip that ships on the bar, so its row offers the
# other direction.
expect screen contains "Hide from top bar"
key esc
# Claude Code's: the sessions submenu, the usage pane, the login, the
# profiles. Enter on Usage opens the pane.
rightclick 4 8
expect screen contains "New session"
expect screen contains "Usage"
expect screen contains "Login"
expect screen contains "Configure profiles"
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "Claude usage"
# Show on top bar persists: the row menu's last item writes the home
# config, and the toast names it.
rightclick 4 8
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "Claude Code: shown on the top bar"
